WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:02.800
Misa was kind of weird that day.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:07.020
The speed at which she cast her Codes at me... Their sharpness...

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.530
They were real Codes, posing mortal harm.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.870
Misa disappeared,

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.920
as though running away from the danger.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.510
If that's true, she may still be alive.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.680
According to Soshiro,

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.170
there's a place she used to go, in case of emergency.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.010
I'm at that place right now.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.950
I'm in Akihabara.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:42.300
Hey!

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.460
Did you find my sister?

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:48.610
Why

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.450
are you...

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.240
Hey, Yumiko!

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.730
Haunting time!

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:09.750
Soshiro-san took off.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.220
You saw that, too, didn't you, Kaho-chan?

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:17.420
Saw what?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.840
The ghostscript of Misa-san.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:24.940
How've ya been?

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.200
Misa-san...

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.770
You're transparent.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.270
You two, wait here.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.610
I'm going to give that thief a piece of my mind!

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.640
Okay, see you later.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.780
Did Misa-san give you that amulet?

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.860
It was in my mailbox.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.370
I wonder if Misa-san sent it.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.990
If you think of the conditions a ghostscript requires to come about,

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:55.460
I believe it's quite unlikely.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.280
What do you mean?

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.730
You'll get scared, so I don't think I'll tell you.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.670
Hey, Kaho-chan!

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.480
You're...

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.070
You're...

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:12.350
How can you be smiling like that?!

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.240
I can hear you without your being so loud.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.410
I'm not sure what you mean...

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:25.960
You know what it means for there to be a ghostscript of you, right?

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:26.700
Huh?

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.730
Well, if I'm dead,

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.450
there's no point in trying to do something about it now.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.700
We haven't found your body.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.710
If you aren't going to look, who is?

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.790
That's why I have been looking.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:48.260
My only memories begin from the moment I came into existence as a ghostscript.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.310
I have no clue where my body might have gone.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.590
That's so irresponsible!

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:55.380
What is?

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.360
I'm kinda getting the sense our conversation isn't really matching up...

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.680
What are you saying?

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.490
I'm talking to Misa right now!

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.410
My sister isn't anywhere around here.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.790
She is! She's right beside you!

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:14.870
Is talking into thin-air popular now?

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.120
Does that mean...

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:19.880
Yep!

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.350
Soshiro can't see or hear me.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:27.980
But you're such a strong ghostscript, anyone should be able to see you.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:31.390
Maybe my cooking has something to do with it.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:40.160
Years ago, I'd stand in for our mother and cook for him. But I wasn't that good...

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:44.550
This is bad.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:52.420
So I used magic to stimulate the parts of the mouth that make food taste good.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:58.270
Soshiro was still pretty young,

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:01.310
so if it was good, even if the ingredients were strange,

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:04.330
he didn't think anything of it.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:06.800
More, please!

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:13.550
Ever since he was young, he's eaten food drenched in magic.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:21.160
Long ago, an emperor started taking poison at an early age to avoid dying from it.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.360
Maybe it's something like that?

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.700
A resistance to magic?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.600
I guess so.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:32.390
Hey, how long do you plan to keep talking to the air?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.970
Wait here.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:41.710
Sorry about that.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.610
What are you doing?

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:57.920
Oh, good idea.

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:01.830
Hey, Soshiro!

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.020
What's this?

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:05.180
It's Misa's voice.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:07.620
I'm transcoding it with magic.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.140
That's right.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:12.430
Don't use my sister's voice. It's creepy.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.820
Also, don't talk about magic around me.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.830
You're pretty stubborn.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:20.680
There's no real reason for me to make you believe magic exists,

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:24.330
but it's cold fact that this is Misa's voice.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.420
It's still possible you're just mimicking her voice.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:31.670
In that case, why not ask something that only you and Misa would know?

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:36.380
How about you tell me the name of that essay you wrote about food.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:37.610
Huh?

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:41.270
Can't tell me? Thought so.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:46.970
That wasn't an essay about food.
It was a thesis from Nippon Physics University.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:48.650
I didn't ask that.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.280
Fine.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.860
The title was "Why Do People Pour Curry Over Fried Cutlets?"

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.850
Believe me now?

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.640
S-Seriously?

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:03.630
I wonder where Soshiro-san went.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:08.180
I'm hungry.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.640
How about curry?

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.630
If we're going to eat,

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.360
I'd prefer something from a restaurant than a vending machine.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:16.760
Oh.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:17.640
What?

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.650
It's a human-vanishing Code.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.650
Maybe this is...

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:30.900
So basically,

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:35.370
this man named Huang revived Guibarthez

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:39.460
and is attempting to use him to revive the Sorceress's Library.

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:42.660
Yeah! That's no good, is it?

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:47.660
I get what's going on, but there's still one thing I can't figure out.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:48.670
What's that?

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:53.950
If we must prevent the Sorceress's Library from being reassembled,

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:57.890
why did we have to try to kill each other?

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:03.660
If you really wanted Kerykeion and me to stay away from that trap-filled building,

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:06.490
you could have just said so.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:12.530
Or you could have taken me down with one of those underhanded tricks of yours.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:15.020
There were multiple solutions.

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:19.900
The way you acted is a complete mystery to me.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:23.920
It's almost like you tried to die deliberately.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.420
What are you even talking about?

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:30.150
Yumiko, do you like magic?

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:34.920
I neither like nor dislike it. Magic is me.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:41.310
Magic is Ichinose Yumiko Cristina. And Ichinose Yumiko Cristina is magic.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:45.510
I see. I guess you could say that.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:48.670
But magic isn't infinite.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:50.920
It may differ from all the tools you've seen before,

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:52.560
but it remains a tool, nonetheless.

00:09:53.930 --> 00:10:02.630
We use those tools and choose the best option among them.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:05.080
We always select the best path.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.320
That goes without saying.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:13.340
But it's also possible that magic may, instead, limit our choices.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:14.980
And when would that happen?

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:22.020
When magic shows you an ideal solution that you couldn't have seen without it.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:27.730
Then, all you can do is select that best option.

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:30.900
Well, I guess it depends on the person.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.060
What would you do?

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:36.260
I'd pick the best option.

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:40.320
I'm glad you said that.

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:47.580
I'm surprised that such a great mage as yourself

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:50.790
would be forced by a child to withdraw.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.010
Don't be fooled by appearances.

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:57.500
Six years ago, the girl I mistook for Anehara Misa...

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:17.530
She

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:21.580
has the ability to dispel any Code.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:24.930
If you relax your guard, it will end poorly for you.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:30.140
I see. So you learned from experience?

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.500
That's right.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.240
Not to mention that the Code abnormality we just saw...

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.230
I'm not sure what it was.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.000
To bring back the Sorceress's Library,

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:45.470
I want to double-check everything and eliminate any uncertain elements.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:50.310
Then we should just...

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:59.010
destroy anyone who resists.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:04.400
What was that?

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:10.630
Guibarthez!

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:16.140
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.640
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.730
I won't make it with the Protection Code.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:35.860
What was that?

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:38.120
What a mess...

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.750
It's that damned thief! I won't let you get away this time!

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.260
Wait!

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:52.660
Transform to swords, my Code.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:54.860
Soshiro!

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:01.380
You bastard!

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.510
Why?

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.590
No way! That should have been fatal!

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:11.350
Understand now? You damned thief!

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.740
H-Hello?

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.580
Um, excuse me!

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:30.740
Is there anyone here?

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.810
Excuse me!

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:35.860
Come in.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:43.990
Misa-san!

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:48.260
Welcome. Good job making it here.

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:53.780
How can he move if he took a direct hit from the Code of Swords?

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:57.110
Are you a mage, too?

00:13:57.110 --> 00:13:58.640
Don't mess with me.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:01.360
Don't compare me to those nut jobs.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:04.850
Why is he unhurt?

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:09.270
A mage-killer?

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:10.870
What is that?

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:19.260
Something the church came up with, a terrifying assassin designed to combat powerful mages.

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:21.510
That's what they're called.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:23.000
That's what this boy is?

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:28.460
From the time they're born, everything they eat contains high-level Codes.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:33.160
Before they completely absorb this world's laws, their Code-infused existences

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:36.020
begin to fluctuate.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:41.620
Most die in youth, their own existences weakening,

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:49.040
but those who develop a Code-resistance end up reflecting all parallel worlds' laws.

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:53.280
That's a mage-killer...

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.040
You've gone and done it now, Anehara Misa!

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:59.540
As a result, that's what he is.

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:04.070
If something happens, have Soshiro help you.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.560
He's my final weapon.

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:09.550
So that's what she meant?

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:14.080
Mages are even in the process of becoming extinct in this age.

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:17.050
I'd never have thought we'd see a mage-killer.

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:21.260
Surprised, right? Magic won't work on my brother.

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:23.050
Give up?

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:24.810
What are you saying?

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:27.660
We've got ourselves another irregularity.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:28.820
What should we do?

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.940
I can handle the mage.

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:35.010
All you have to do is handle the mage-killer.

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:38.240
I see. I guess we could do that, too.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:45.090
I might not have mentioned it, but I'm trained in Chinese kempo.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:47.040
Oh, I see.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:50.940
Looks like one punch might not have been enough.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.870
My brother is strong!

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.850
Thanks for the advice.

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:58.620
How about we get started, as well?

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:00.350
Let's.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.100
Sounds about right to me.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:09.660
You two found this place pretty handily.

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:13.230
We just found your Code by chance.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:17.330
Um, are you okay?

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:20.620
I can't really say that I am...

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.960
I took quite a bit of damage.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:27.520
But! But I'm glad I got to see you!

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:31.790
Yumiko-chan and Soshiro-san were worried about you.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:37.300
Oh, yeah! I have to tell Yumiko-chan I found you!

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:46.370
You're good.

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:49.020
You're not going to use that sword?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:53.050
No, this is an important magical sword.

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:55.910
It'd be a problem if it broke in a moment of carelessness.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.770
What do you mean, "magical"?

00:16:57.770 --> 00:16:59.580
You're nuts!

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:02.440
Die!

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:06.910
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.990
I won't let you escape!

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:20.590
Take this!

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:34.360
Looks like you weren't even worth the effort.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.250
Damn you...

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:40.290
Misa, leave the rest to me.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:41.930
Go to Soshiro.

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:43.220
You're right.

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:45.920
Don't count me out!

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:50.750
It's useless!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.620
It's over now!

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:16.990
I'm stronger than I was six years ago.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.640
Morishita Koyomi

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:24.970
Hello?

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:26.150
Is this Koyomi?

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:28.630
Yumiko-chan, where are you now?

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:30.370
We found Misa-san!

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:31.850
Really?

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:34.080
Is Misa okay?

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:37.170
Yeah. She's hurt, but she's fine.

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:39.660
I'm glad...

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:42.470
Transform to swords, my Code.

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:51.190
I told you not to count me out.

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:02.220
Yumiko-chan?

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:04.720
Are you there? Yumiko-chan?

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:07.070
Huh?

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:08.820
What's wrong?

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:11.610
Suddenly, I couldn't hear anything.

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:14.310
Maybe it broke?

00:19:14.310 --> 00:19:16.750
I don't think shaking will help it.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:18.220
Hey, who's there?

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:22.010
Uh, Soshiro-san?

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:23.600
Um...

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:26.740
I know who it is. Don't say any more.

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:29.030
I'm sort of in the midst of something right now.

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.980
U-Um... Um...

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.120
We found Misa-san.

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:35.090
Then bring her here now!

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:37.150
The idiot collapsed and is bleeding!

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:38.650
Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:39.570
Huh?!

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.260
Don't make me say it twice!

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:42.300
I'll tell you where I am now.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:43.480
Hurry it up!

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:54.090
There's a human-vanishing Code up.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:55.660
Over there.

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:07.150
Kaho-chan, wh-wh-wh-wh-what should we do?

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:08.320
Ichinose.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:14.460
Yumiko-chan!

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:17.000
Get your act together!

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:20.990
Yumiko-chan...

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:23.340
What should we do, Soshiro-san?

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:24.380
Calm down.

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:27.350
Damn, is the ambulance here yet?

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:28.830
Yumiko-chan!

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:30.750
Hold on, Yumiko-chan!

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:34.250
Please! Wake up.

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:37.710
Open your eyes!

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:43.240
Y-Yumiko-chan?

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:56.230
Yumiko-

00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.400
chan.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:30.850
It's finally begun...

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:45.200
So, she revived?

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:49.040
That's the legendary sorceress.

00:21:58.450 --> 00:22:02.520
Digitalis Flammalacia.

00:23:45.650 --> 00:23:48.900
In order to defeat the now-revived legendary sorceress,

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:53.060
the Modern-Day mage will sacrifice Ichinose Yumiko,

00:23:53.060 --> 00:23:56.710
believing it to be the sole "best" method.

00:23:56.710 --> 00:24:00.000
At that moment, the apprentice mage will...

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:06.980
Sakazaki   Kaho

00:24:07.890 --> 00:24:11.420
Hello! Morishita Koyomi here!

00:24:11.420 --> 00:24:14.400
Hi! Anehara Misa here!

00:24:14.400 --> 00:24:16.830
Today, we have fan letters.

00:24:18.340 --> 00:24:21.790
This letter is from the nameless writer in Tokyo,

00:24:21.790 --> 00:24:24.530
"I-Love-Telecasters."

00:24:24.530 --> 00:24:29.080
"Hello, the two of you. I like Kaho-chan a lot.

00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:33.190
I want to learn more about her."

00:24:33.190 --> 00:24:36.200
How about we call Kaho-chan, then?

00:24:36.200 --> 00:24:38.560
Kaho-chan!

00:24:38.950 --> 00:24:40.600
Hallo, hallo.

00:24:40.600 --> 00:24:42.400
CQ. CQ.

00:24:42.400 --> 00:24:44.610
Huh, where are you?

00:24:44.610 --> 00:24:46.510
I can hear you, but...

00:24:46.510 --> 00:24:50.810
Unfortunately, due to the financial crisis caused by sub-prime mortgages,

00:24:50.810 --> 00:24:53.820
we're currently in the midst of a budget cut.

00:24:53.820 --> 00:24:59.980
You basically seem to be trying to save face, but you weren't made into a puppet.

00:24:59.980 --> 00:25:02.100
How embarrassing.

00:25:02.100 --> 00:25:10.280
Kaho-chan, a fan wrote that they like you a lot and want to know more about you.

00:25:10.280 --> 00:25:13.190
I'm excited now.

00:25:13.190 --> 00:25:18.660
But it seems like you know a lot.

00:25:18.660 --> 00:25:22.050
To be honest, it's due to all the surfing I do.

00:25:23.470 --> 00:25:26.450
So you go surfing?

00:25:27.370 --> 00:25:30.710
But I don't think that has anything to do with knowing a lot...

00:25:30.710 --> 00:25:34.900
Morishita, I think that's wrong on a fundamental level.

00:25:34.900 --> 00:25:36.920
Huh? Huh? What?

00:25:36.920 --> 00:25:39.960
Oh, it looks like we're out of time.

00:25:39.960 --> 00:25:44.670
We'll give you the last bit of time to promote yourself.

00:25:46.900 --> 00:25:49.400
Stain me in your colors.

00:25:49.970 --> 00:25:51.480
Just kidding!

00:25:51.740 --> 00:25:53.020
Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:25:53.020 --> 00:25:54.890
What's that?

00:25:54.890 --> 00:25:59.950
So essentially, we figured out that we can't really figure out anything about her.

00:25:59.950 --> 00:26:01.110
Heh heh?

00:26:01.110 --> 00:26:02.850
Morishita, don't worry about it.

00:26:02.850 --> 00:26:07.200
Next time is the last ep. Let's study together then, too!

00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:08.270
Bye-bye!

00:26:08.270 --> 00:26:09.490
Later.
